	'benefits' => "Nothing to install | Staff and customers only need a modern browser\nSecure logins and permissions | Access is controlled by role, and sensitive actions are logged\nWorks on phones and tablets | Responsive screens suit people working away from a desk\nConnects to your tools | Payment, messaging and accounting services can be connected through APIs\nStraightforward to extend | New modules can be added without rebuilding what already works",
	'workflow' => "Define the users and tasks | We list who will use the system and the jobs they need to get done.\nModel the data | We design how information is stored, because a sound data structure saves problems later.\nPrototype the main screens | You click through the key steps before the build starts.\nBuild in stages | Core features arrive first, followed by reports and integrations.\nTest security and load | We check permissions, input handling and how the system behaves with realistic data.\nDeploy and monitor | We set up hosting, backups and error monitoring, then support the launch.",
	'use_cases' => "A customer portal for orders, documents or service requests\nAn internal system for bookings, approvals or field staff\nA booking or appointment platform for a service business\nAn admin dashboard that brings data from several sources together",
	'faqs' => "What is the difference between a website and a web application? | A website mainly presents information. A web application lets users log in and work with data, such as placing an order or updating a record.\nCan it work on mobile phones? | Yes. We design screens to work well in phone browsers. If you need device features or an app store presence, a mobile app may also make sense.\nHow do you keep the data secure? | We use role-based access, encrypted connections, protection against common attacks such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting, and regular backups.\nCan you take over an existing application? | Often, yes. We review the code and hosting first, then tell you plainly whether improving it or rebuilding parts of it makes more sense.",
	'cta_text' => 'Describe the task your team or customers are struggling with, and we will sketch out what a web application could do.',
	'related_services' => 'api-development-integration,ui-ux-design,cloud-solutions',
