'ui-ux-design' => array(
	'title' => 'UI/UX Design',
	'headline' => 'Clear Screens and Journeys That People Understand First Time',
	'description' => "<p>When people cannot work out what to do on a screen, they rarely complain. They leave the website, or they ring your office, or they go back to the old spreadsheet. Good UI/UX design removes that friction before it costs you customers or wastes staff time.</p><p>We design interfaces by starting from the task someone is trying to finish. That means simple wireframes first, testing with real people where possible, and visual design that follows your brand while staying readable, accessible and usable on a phone.</p>",
	'problems' => "New staff need constant help with the system | We reorganise screens around real tasks, so that the next step is clear without training.\nVisitors do not complete the form | We cut unnecessary fields, improve the wording and show helpful error messages.\nThe product looks inconsistent | A small set of reusable design components makes every screen feel like one product.\nText is hard to read on a phone | We check text size, contrast and touch targets on real small screens.",
	'benefits' => "User journeys | Clear maps show how people move through the task and where they get stuck\nWireframes | Layouts can be agreed cheaply before any code is written\nClickable prototypes | You can try the flow and collect feedback before development\nAccessible design | Sensible contrast, labels and keyboard use help more people use your product\nDeveloper-ready designs | Specifications that our own developers or yours can build from",
	'workflow' => "Listen to users | We talk to customers or staff about what they are trying to achieve.\nReview what exists | We look for the points where people get confused or give up.\nSketch the journey | Simple flows and wireframes show the proposed path.\nPrototype | We build a clickable version of the important screens.\nTest and refine | We watch people use it, then fix what confuses them.\nDesign and hand over | We complete the visual design and prepare it for development.",
	'use_cases' => "A web application that staff find confusing\nA new product that needs its screens worked out before coding begins\nA website with plenty of visitors but few enquiries\nAn older system that needs a modern, consistent interface",
	'faqs' => "What is the difference between UI and UX? | UX is how the whole experience works for the person using it. UI is what they see and touch on the screen. Both have to be right for a product to feel easy.\nDo I need UX design for a small project? | A light version is usually enough: a short review of the main tasks and simple wireframes can prevent expensive changes later.\nCan you redesign without rebuilding everything? | Often, yes. We can improve the most important screens first, and leave the rest until it is worthwhile.\nWill you test with real users? | Wherever we can get access to them. Even a few short sessions usually reveal the biggest problems.",
	'cta_text' => 'If people struggle with your website or software, send us the link and we will take a look.',
	'related_services' => 'web-application-development,website-development,mobile-app-development',
	'form_label' => 'UI/UX Design',
	'seo' => array('UI/UX Design Services for Websites & Apps | GIRZOCK', 'User journeys, wireframes and interface design that make websites and business software easier to use. UI/UX design by GIRZOCK Technologies.', 'UI UX design services'),
),

