'cloud-solutions' => array(
	'title' => 'Cloud Computing Solutions',
	'headline' => 'Practical Cloud Solutions Without the Jargon',
	'description' => "<p>Moving to the cloud should solve a specific problem: a server that keeps slowing down, backups that depend on someone remembering them, or a team that needs access from more than one location. Moved without a plan, a business can simply end up with the same problems and a larger monthly bill.</p><p>We help you decide what belongs in the cloud, choose a provider that suits the workload, and move in steps that can be reversed if something goes wrong. Afterwards you get clear monitoring and backups, along with a straightforward explanation of what you are paying for.</p>",
	'problems' => "Your website slows down when it gets busy | Cloud hosting lets capacity be sized to real demand instead of guessed in advance.\nBackups are manual, or nobody has checked them | We automate backups and test that they can actually be restored.\nAn office server is a single point of failure | Moving services off one machine reduces the damage if it fails.\nThe cloud bill keeps growing | We review what is running, remove what is idle and size the rest properly.",
	'benefits' => "A clear assessment | Know what should move, what should stay and why\nStaged migration | Moves are done in steps, with a rollback plan at each one\nAutomated backups | Regular, tested copies held separately from the live system\nMonitoring and alerts | Problems are spotted before customers report them\nCost visibility | A plain explanation of what you are paying for",
	'workflow' => "Assess what you have | We list your applications, data, traffic and pain points.\nChoose the platform | We compare options based on your workload and budget, not on fashion.\nPlan the move | We agree the order, the downtime and how to roll back.\nMigrate in stages | The least risky parts go first, and each is checked before the next.\nSet up operations | Backups, monitoring and access controls go in before we finish.\nReview costs | After things have settled, we adjust the sizing to what is really used.",
	'use_cases' => "A growing website or application that has outgrown shared hosting\nA business that relies on one office server\nA company with staff who need secure remote access\nA team with cloud costs it no longer understands",
	'faqs' => "Is the cloud always cheaper? | Not always. It is often better value for workloads that change or need resilience, but a steady small site may be fine on simpler hosting. We will tell you which applies.\nIs my data safe in the cloud? | Major providers offer strong security, but correct configuration remains your responsibility. We set up access controls, encryption and backups accordingly.\nWill there be downtime during the move? | It depends on the system. Many moves can be scheduled for quiet periods with little disruption, and we agree this with you beforehand.\nWhich cloud provider do you recommend? | It depends on what you run. We often work with AWS, covered on our AWS page, and we will consider other options where they fit better.",
	'cta_text' => 'If your hosting or backups worry you, tell us what you run today and we will review it.',
	'related_services' => 'aws-cloud-solutions,website-maintenance-support,it-consulting',
	'form_label' => 'Cloud & AWS Solutions',
	'seo' => array('Cloud Computing Solutions for Businesses | GIRZOCK', 'Cloud planning, migration, backups and monitoring for growing businesses. Honest advice on what to move and what it costs, from GIRZOCK Technologies.', 'cloud computing solutions'),
),

'aws-cloud-solutions' => array(
	'title' => 'AWS Cloud Solutions',
	'headline' => 'Reliable Hosting and Infrastructure on Amazon Web Services',
	'description' => "<p>Amazon Web Services offers an enormous range of services, and that range is exactly what makes it easy to overspend or leave something insecure. Most businesses need only a handful of those services, set up carefully.</p><p>We design, deploy and support applications on AWS, typically starting with familiar building blocks such as virtual servers (EC2), managed databases (RDS), file storage (S3) and monitoring (CloudWatch). We set access permissions tightly, keep your account in your own name, and document what we have built so that you are never dependent on one person's memory.</p>",
	'problems' => "A single server takes the whole site down | We can separate the application and database, and add resilience where it is justified.\nThe AWS bill is a mystery | We review usage, remove what is idle and set up budget alerts.\nThe account was set up quickly and never reviewed | We check permissions, public access and logging, then fix the gaps.\nDeployments are manual and nerve-racking | A repeatable process reduces the chance of mistakes when you release changes.",
	'benefits' => "Architecture to suit you | No more complexity than your application needs\nSecure configuration | Least-privilege access and locked-down public exposure\nManaged databases and backups | Less routine administration and dependable recovery\nBudget alerts | Warnings before a surprise on your monthly bill\nClear documentation | You know what exists and why it is there",
	'workflow' => "Review the application | We look at what it does, its traffic and how much downtime you can accept.\nDesign the setup | We keep the design as simple as the requirements allow.\nBuild the environment | We set up accounts, networks, servers, databases and storage.\nMigrate and test | We move the application and data, checking each stage against a rollback plan.\nAdd operations | Monitoring, alerts and backups are put in place and tested.\nHand over | You receive documentation and, if you wish, ongoing support.",
	'use_cases' => "An application moving from shared hosting or a single server\nA growing product that needs better reliability\nAn existing AWS account that needs a security and cost review\nA business that needs dependable backup and recovery",
	'faqs' => "Who owns the AWS account? | You should. We work with the access you grant, and it can be removed at any time. That way, your infrastructure always stays under your control.\nIs AWS overkill for a small business? | It can be. For a simple website, standard hosting may be better value, and we will say so if that is your situation.\nCan you reduce our current AWS costs? | We can review your usage and find unused or oversized resources. How much can be saved depends on your setup.\nDo you offer ongoing AWS support? | Yes. We can handle monitoring, updates and changes after launch, on terms we agree with you.",
	'cta_text' => 'Already on AWS or thinking about it? Tell us your situation and we will suggest a next step.',
	'related_services' => 'cloud-solutions,web-application-development,it-consulting',
	'menu_title' => 'AWS Cloud Solutions',
	'menu_description' => 'Reliable hosting and infrastructure on Amazon Web Services.',
	'menu_image' => $I.'service/core-8.png',
	'menu_order' => 10,
	'seo' => array('AWS Cloud Solutions: Migration & Support | GIRZOCK', 'AWS architecture, migration, cost reviews and ongoing support for growing businesses, delivered by GIRZOCK Technologies from Tamil Nadu.', 'AWS cloud solutions'),
),

'api-development-integration' => array(
	'title' => 'API Development & Integration',
	'headline' => 'Connect Your Systems So People Stop Copying Data Between Them',
	'description' => "<p>Most businesses end up with several systems that do not talk to each other: a website, an accounting package, a payment gateway, a messaging service, perhaps a CRM. Someone ends up copying information from one to another, and that is where the delays and typing mistakes come in.</p><p>An API is the agreed way for two systems to exchange data automatically. We connect the tools you already use and build new APIs for your own applications, paying close attention to the unglamorous parts: what happens if a service is down, how errors get reported, and who is allowed to access what.</p>",
	'problems' => "Staff re-enter website orders into accounts | An integration passes each order across automatically, with fewer errors.\nPayment status has to be checked by hand | Payment gateway notifications can update the order as soon as a payment succeeds or fails.\nYour app needs data held in another system | A secure API lets your apps share data without giving out direct database access.\nAn integration fails silently | We add logging, retries and alerts, so failures are noticed and resolved.",
	'benefits' => "Payment gateway integration | Reliable handling of payments, failures and refunds\nMessaging and email | Send notifications through approved SMS, email and WhatsApp providers\nAccounting and CRM connections | Reduce double entry between business systems\nCustom REST APIs | Well-structured, documented access to your own data\nMonitoring and retries | Failures are recorded and retried instead of being lost",
	'workflow' => "Map the data flow | We work out what moves between systems, when, and which one is the source of truth.\nCheck the other side | We review the provider's documentation, limits and costs.\nDesign the contract | We agree on the data format, authentication and error handling.\nBuild with safeguards | We add validation, logging and retries from the start.\nTest failure cases | We test timeouts, duplicates and bad data, not only the happy path.\nDocument and monitor | You get documentation and alerts for when something needs attention.",
	'use_cases' => "Connecting a website or store to accounting software\nAdding a payment gateway or messaging service to an application\nFeeding a mobile app from a central system\nReplacing a manual daily export and import between systems",
	'faqs' => "What is an API, in simple terms? | It is an agreed way for one piece of software to request data or actions from another, without a person doing it by hand.\nCan any two systems be connected? | Many can, but it depends on what access each one provides. We check this early, and tell you if there is a limit.\nAre there ongoing costs? | Some providers charge by usage or subscription. We identify those costs before we build.\nWhat happens if the other service goes down? | We design for it, usually by queuing work and retrying, then alerting someone if the problem continues.",
	'cta_text' => 'Tell us which systems you wish talked to each other, and we will check what is possible.',
	'related_services' => 'web-application-development,crm-business-management-software,custom-software-development',
	'image' => $I.'feature/software-3.png',
	'icon' => $I.'feature/feature7.svg',
	'short_description' => 'Connect payment, messaging, accounting and business systems, so that people stop copying data by hand.',
	'page_layout' => 'feature',
	'page_order' => 12,
	'menu_title' => 'API Development',
	'menu_description' => 'Connect your systems so people stop copying data by hand.',
	'menu_image' => $I.'project/pro8-15.png',
	'menu_order' => 13,
	'footer_title' => 'API Development & Integration',
	'footer_order' => 12,
	'form_label' => 'API Development & Integration',
	'form_order' => 11,
	'seo' => array('API Development & Integration Services | GIRZOCK', 'Connect payment gateways, accounting tools, CRMs and messaging services through reliable APIs, built by GIRZOCK Technologies in Tirunelveli District.', 'API integration services'),
),

'website-maintenance-support' => array(
	'title' => 'Website Maintenance & Technical Support',
	'headline' => 'Keep Your Website Secure, Backed Up and Working',
	'description' => "<p>A website is not finished on launch day. Software needs security updates, forms can stop sending without anyone noticing, certificates expire, and small changes pile up on someone's list. These problems tend to appear at the worst moment, often just when a customer is trying to reach you.</p><p>Our maintenance and support service gives you someone to call. We keep the software updated, check that backups can actually be restored, watch for problems and make small changes when you ask. It is available for websites we built, and for those we did not, after an initial review.</p>",
	'problems' => "The original developer cannot be reached | We review the site, secure access and take over its care.\nThe contact form stopped working and no one noticed | Regular checks of forms and key pages catch silent failures.\nThe site has been hacked or shows warnings | We clean it up, find the likely cause and improve its protection.\nSmall changes never get done | You have a clear route for updates, with a known person handling them.",
	'benefits' => "Software updates | Platform, theme and plugin updates are tested and applied\nTested backups | Backups are stored separately, and restores are tried in practice\nSecurity checks | Regular reviews help find problems early\nUptime and form checks | Problems are noticed before too many customers run into them\nContent changes | Small updates are handled without a new project each time",
	'workflow' => "Review the site | We check its age, hosting, plugins, backups and access details.\nFix the urgent issues | Anything exposing you to immediate risk comes first.\nAgree the plan | We set out how often updates and checks happen, and what is included.\nRun routine care | Updates, backups and checks follow the agreed schedule.\nHandle requests | You send changes or problems to us, and we respond as agreed.\nReport back | You get a plain summary of what was done.",
	'use_cases' => "A business website with no one looking after it\nA WordPress site that is rarely updated\nAn online store where downtime directly costs sales\nA company whose previous developer is no longer available",
	'faqs' => "Do you maintain sites that you did not build? | Yes, usually. We review the site first, because some old or heavily modified sites need repairs before they can be maintained safely.\nHow often should a website be updated? | Security updates should be applied soon after release, and routine checks should happen at least monthly. The right rhythm depends on the platform and how much the site changes.\nWhat if my site goes down at night? | Tell us what level of response your business needs, and we will set clear expectations in the support plan.\nDo I need maintenance for a simple site? | Even a simple site needs backups, updates and renewals. A static site usually requires less work than WordPress or a store.",
	'cta_text' => 'If nobody is looking after your website, send us the address and we will review it.',
	'related_services' => 'wordpress-development,cloud-solutions,seo-services',
	'image' => $I.'feature/software-4.png',
	'icon' => $I.'feature/feature8.svg',
	'short_description' => 'Updates, tested backups, security checks and small changes, so that your website keeps working.',
	'page_layout' => 'feature',
	'page_order' => 13,
	'menu_title' => 'Website Maintenance',
	'menu_description' => 'Updates, tested backups and security checks for your website.',
	'menu_image' => $I.'event/hero4.png',
	'menu_order' => 14,
	'footer_title' => 'Website Maintenance & Support',
	'footer_order' => 13,
	'form_label' => 'Website Maintenance & Support',
	'form_order' => 12,
	'seo' => array('Website Maintenance & Technical Support | GIRZOCK', 'Website updates, tested backups, security checks and small changes for businesses in Tirunelveli and Tamil Nadu. Support from GIRZOCK Technologies.', 'website maintenance services'),
),

'seo-services' => array(
	'title' => 'Search Engine Optimization (SEO)',
	'headline' => 'Honest SEO That Helps Local Customers Find You',
	'description' => "<p>SEO is mostly about making it easy for search engines to understand your business, and giving people useful answers when they get there. For a local business, Google says results depend largely on three things: relevance, distance and prominence. You can influence the first and last of these far more than most businesses do.</p><p>We focus on foundations that last: technical health, clear service pages, a well-kept Google Business Profile, and content that answers real questions. We do not sell guaranteed rankings, spam backlinks or fake reviews. No one can honestly promise a position on Google, and those shortcuts can damage a business in the long run.</p>",
	'problems' => "Your business does not appear for local searches | We review your site and Google Business Profile, and improve how clearly they describe what you do and where.\nThe website has only a few thin pages | We plan pages around the services and questions customers actually search for.\nThe site is slow or has technical errors | We find and fix crawl errors, broken links and slow pages.\nYou paid for SEO and saw only vague reports | We explain what we changed and why, and report on enquiries and traffic you can verify.",
	'benefits' => "Technical SEO audit | Crawling, indexing, speed and structured data are reviewed\nOn-page improvements | Better titles, headings, descriptions and internal links\nLocal SEO | Google Business Profile guidance and consistent business details\nContent planning | Topics based on what your customers really ask\nHonest reporting | Search Console and analytics data that you can check yourself",
	'workflow' => "Audit the starting point | We review your site, profile, search visibility and any past SEO work.\nUnderstand search intent | We work out what customers type, and what they want when they do.\nFix the foundations | Technical problems and unclear pages come first.\nImprove key pages | We strengthen your main service and location information.\nCreate useful content | We publish content only where it can really help a reader.\nMeasure and adjust | We watch Search Console and analytics, then decide what to do next.",
	'use_cases' => "A local business that cannot be found for its main services\nA new website that needs to start with sound foundations\nA business moving to a new site without wanting to lose search traffic\nA company unhappy with vague SEO reports",
	'faqs' => "Can you guarantee first-page rankings? | No, and be careful of anyone who does. Rankings depend on competition, your site's authority, Google's systems and other factors outside anyone's direct control.\nHow long does SEO take? | Technical fixes can take effect soon after pages are recrawled, but meaningful results often take months, depending on competition and how much work is needed.\nDo I need a Google Business Profile? | If you serve local customers, yes. It is free, and Google uses it for local results. It must represent your real business accurately.\nShould I create a page for every town? | Only where you have something genuinely useful to say about it. Near-identical city pages are treated as spam and rarely help.",
	'cta_text' => 'Send us your website address and the services you most want to be found for.',
	'related_services' => 'website-development,website-maintenance-support,wordpress-development',
	'image' => $I.'feature/software-5.png',
	'icon' => $I.'feature/feature3-1.svg',
	'short_description' => 'Technical SEO, clear service pages and local search guidance, with honest reporting and no ranking guarantees.',
	'page_layout' => 'feature',
	'page_order' => 14,
	'menu_title' => 'SEO Services',
	'menu_description' => 'Honest technical and local SEO, with no ranking guarantees.',
	'menu_image' => $I.'event/faq3.png',
	'menu_order' => 15,
	'footer_title' => 'Search Engine Optimization',
	'footer_order' => 14,
	'form_label' => 'Search Engine Optimization (SEO)',
	'form_order' => 13,
	'seo' => array('SEO Services in Tirunelveli & Tamil Nadu | GIRZOCK', 'Technical SEO, local search guidance and honest reporting for businesses in Tirunelveli and Tamil Nadu. No guaranteed-ranking promises or spam links.', 'SEO services in Tirunelveli'),
),

'digital-transformation' => array(
	'title' => 'Digital Transformation & Business Automation',
	'headline' => 'Replace Repetitive Manual Work, One Practical Step at a Time',
	'description' => "<p>Digital transformation sounds like a large programme that only big companies can afford. For most businesses it is simpler than that: find the task that wastes the most time, fix it properly, and then do the same with the next one.</p><p>We help you identify where paper, re-typing and chasing people are costing you the most, then automate those steps using tools you already have wherever possible. New software is only recommended when it is really needed. Our article on <a href=\"site:blog/a-practical-first-step-towards-digital-transformation\">a practical first step</a> shows how to begin.</p>",
	'problems' => "Staff spend hours on repetitive data entry | We connect systems and automate the routine steps, so people can spend that time on customers.\nApprovals depend on paper moving between desks | Digital forms and notifications show every request and who needs to act.\nReports take days to compile | Information held in one place can produce reports automatically.\nTechnology was bought but never properly used | We look at what you already own, because better use of it may be the cheapest step.",
	'benefits' => "A clear starting point | Priorities based on time and money actually lost\nProcess automation | Routine tasks run with less manual effort and fewer errors\nConnected systems | Data flows between tools instead of being retyped\nTraining and adoption | Staff are helped through the change, not simply handed a new tool\nStep-by-step investment | Each stage is judged on its results before the next begins",
	'workflow' => "Find the bottlenecks | We talk to staff and follow the work through the business.\nEstimate the value | We compare effort saved against the cost of each possible fix.\nChoose one first step | We pick something visible, useful and low risk.\nImplement and train | We configure or build the solution, and help people adopt it.\nMeasure the result | We compare before and after, using figures agreed in advance.\nRepeat | We move to the next priority, using what we have learned.",
	'use_cases' => "A family business still run on paper registers\nA growing company with processes that no longer scale\nAn institution moving records and forms online\nA business that wants to reduce repetitive administrative work",
	'faqs' => "Where should a small business start? | With one repetitive task that costs real time each week. An early, visible result makes the next step much easier.\nWill automation replace my staff? | It normally removes repetitive tasks and frees people for work that needs judgement. How you use that time is your decision.\nDo we need to replace all our software? | Rarely. It is often better to connect or make better use of what you have.\nHow do you measure success? | We agree a simple measure before starting, such as hours spent on a task or how quickly enquiries are answered.",
	'cta_text' => 'Tell us the task that wastes the most time in your business, and we will suggest where to begin.',
	'related_services' => 'crm-business-management-software,custom-software-development,it-consulting',
	'short_description' => 'A step-by-step plan to replace paper and repetitive manual work with connected, automated systems.',
	'image' => $I.'bg/bg2.png',
	'icon' => $I.'feature/feature3-2.svg',
	'page_layout' => 'feature',
	'page_order' => 15,
	'footer_title' => 'Digital Transformation',
	'footer_order' => 15,
	'form_label' => 'Digital Transformation & Automation',
	'form_order' => 14,
	'seo' => array('Digital Transformation & Business Automation | GIRZOCK', 'Practical business automation for small and growing companies in Tamil Nadu. Replace paper and repetitive data entry one step at a time.', 'business automation services'),
),

'it-consulting' => array(
	'headline' => 'Independent Technology Advice in Plain Language',
	'description' => "<p>Technology decisions are hard to judge if they are not your daily work. A vendor recommends what it sells, a friend recommends what they have heard about, and the wrong choice can cost far more than the software itself.</p><p>Our IT consulting gives you a straightforward second opinion: what your options are, what each will really cost to run, and which risks matter. Sometimes the honest advice is to keep what you have and fix one small thing. We are happy to say that too.</p>",
	'problems' => "A vendor quote is hard to judge | We review the proposal and explain what you are being offered and what is missing.\nSystems have grown without a plan | We map what you run, and set out a sensible order for improvements.\nYou are unsure whether your data is safe | We look at access, backups and basic security, then list the priorities.\nA software project has gone off track | We review the situation and advise on how to recover it.",
	'benefits' => "Plain-language advice | Clear options and trade-offs, without jargon\nTechnology roadmap | A prioritised plan you can follow at your own pace\nVendor and quote review | A second opinion before you commit money\nBasic security review | The most important risks and how to reduce them\nNo obligation to build | You can use the advice with any provider",
	'workflow' => "Understand your goals | We start with the business decision you are trying to make.\nReview what exists | We look at your systems, contracts and costs.\nSet out the options | We explain realistic choices, with their costs and risks.\nRecommend a direction | We say what we would do and why.\nAgree next steps | You get a short, prioritised plan.\nSupport if needed | We can help carry it out, or brief another provider.",
	'use_cases' => "An owner about to sign a large software contract\nA business without an in-house IT person\nA company planning its next few years of technology spending\nA team recovering from a failed software project",
	'faqs' => "Do I have to use GIRZOCK to build what you recommend? | No. The advice is yours to use with any provider.\nIs consulting worthwhile for a small business? | A short review can be worthwhile if you are about to make a large or long-term commitment.\nWhat do I need to prepare? | Any relevant quotes, contracts and a description of what is not working. We will ask for anything else we need.\nCan you talk directly with our current vendor? | Yes, if you would like us to. It often clears up technical questions quickly.",
	'cta_text' => 'Facing a technology decision? Tell us about it before you commit.',
	'related_services' => 'digital-transformation,cloud-solutions,custom-software-development',
	'form_label' => 'IT Consulting',
	'seo' => array('IT Consulting for Small Businesses in Tamil Nadu | GIRZOCK', 'Independent, plain-language technology advice: vendor reviews, roadmaps and security checks for small businesses in Tirunelveli and Tamil Nadu.', 'IT consulting services'),
),

);
